infographic sequence-roadmap-vertical-plain-text
data
  title Balancing algorithms: blind to load-aware
  desc The further down the spectrum, the more it reacts to real load
  sequences
    - label Round-robin
      desc Even by request count, blind to load — feeds a slow node its even share
    - label Weighted round-robin
      desc Bigger servers get a larger share, still blind to live conditions
    - label Least-connections
      desc Slow node accumulates open connections, naturally stops receiving new ones
    - label Least-response-time / EWMA
      desc Tracks recent latency, prefers the fastest — a 4 s node gets less traffic
    - label Consistent hashing
      desc Same key to same server; remaps only ~1/N of keys on a membership change
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
